16. Protection is a series of fulfillment of the rights of women and child victims of violence and discrimination starting from prevention efforts, handling and empowerment;
17. Prevention is a direct effort carried out by the Regional Government to prevent acts of violence against women and children and Indirect;
18. Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment, hereinafter abbreviated as P2TP2A, is an Integrated Service Unit established by the Regional Government to provide services to women and child victims of violence comprehensively including information services, assistance and legal aid, counseling services, medical services and safe houses through referral;
19. Task Force for Prevention and Handling of Criminal Acts of Trafficking in Persons, hereinafter referred to as Task Force, is a coordinative institution tasked with coordinating prevention and handling efforts of criminal acts of trafficking in persons in Cirebon Regency;
20. Parents are biological father and/or mother, or step father and/or mother, or adoptive father and/or mother;
21. Family is a person who has a blood relationship in a straight line upward or downward and collateral line up to the third degree, or who has a marital relationship, or a person who is a dependent of a woman and/or child;
22. Community is individuals, families, groups, and social organizations and/or community organizations.
23. Child-Friendly Regency is a Regency that has a child rights-based development system through the integration of commitment and resources of government, community, business world and media that are planned comprehensively and sustainably in policies, programs and activities to ensure the fulfillment of children's rights and special protection of children.
24. Private Sector is Non-Governmental Institutions, Business World and Mass Media.

Article 19
(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protection of women and children, cooperation may be conducted with:
a. Central Government;
b. Provincial Government/other Provinces;
c. Regency/City Government;
d. Non-governmental institutions; and
e. Community.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. Exchange of data and information;
b. Recovery of victims of violence;
c. Repatriation and social reintegration;
d. Provision of evidence and witnesses; and
e. Followed up in accordance with applicable law.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be set forth in the form of a Joint Agreement.

