Article 3
The objectives of protection, empowerment of women and children, are to: a. Fulfill the rights of children;
b. Prevent acts of violence against women and children including human trafficking;
c. Eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
d. Protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; e. Provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. Protect children from child marriage and conduct mediation on household disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

Article 17
In addition to establishing the Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A) or other designation as referred to in Article 16, in order to support the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence, the Regent shall establish:
a. Task force on human trafficking;
b. Task force on child marriage prevention;
c. Regional action committee on the elimination of the worst forms of child labor;
d. Task force on child-friendly regency or other designation.

Article 6
Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 5, also obtain special rights, as follows;
a. Right to respect and full utilization for survival, growth and development;
b. Right to basic services;
c. Right to equal protection;
d. Right to be free from various stigma; and
e. Right to obtain freedom.

