CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The protection, empowerment of women and children shall be implemented based on the principles of:
a. Humanity;
b. Justice and gender equality;
c. Shelter;
d. Best interests of victims;
e. Survival of mothers;
f. Survival and development of children;
g. Non-discrimination;
h. Confidentiality of victims;
i. Anti-violence;
j. Empowerment of victims;
k. Holistic.

CHAPTER VII
SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 13
(1) Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence are as follows:
a. Complaint services;
b. Health services;
c. Legal services;
d. Repatriation;
e. Recovery, social reintegration, and medicolegal;
f. Identification services;
g. Psychological services; and
h. Shelter.
(2) Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Government and implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. Social;
b. Economic;
c. Health;
d. Women's empowerment and child protection; and
e. Mental and spiritual.
(3) In carrying out duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with Government Agencies, other Regional Governments, and the community.
(4) Further provisions regarding procedures for handling services for women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2) and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.
